        type: "paragraph",
        text: "There's a meaningful difference between high-volume settlement firms built around processing cases quickly and firms that prioritize genuinely working up each case, gathering full documentation, consulting appropriate experts, understanding the client's specific circumstances, before pushing toward resolution. Clients can often sense the difference, even without understanding the legal mechanics behind it, in how thoroughly their attorney seems to know their case during conversations. A firm that takes the time to work a case properly, even if it takes somewhat longer, tends to produce both stronger outcomes and a client who feels genuinely represented rather than processed.",
