        type: "paragraph",
        text: "The end of a case is one of the most overlooked moments in the entire attorney-client relationship. A clear closing conversation, explaining the final outcome, next steps if any, and an invitation to reach out in the future, leaves a far stronger lasting impression than a case that simply goes quiet after resolution. This final touchpoint is also, not coincidentally, the ideal moment to build the kind of client satisfaction and trust that produces referrals and reviews, since it's the last interaction shaping how a client remembers the entire experience.",
