        text: "Attorney bio pages are some of the most visited, and most neglected, pages on a law firm website. A prospective client who's already interested enough to click on an individual attorney's name is actively evaluating whether this is the person they want handling their legal matter, which makes the bio one of the highest-stakes pieces of content on the entire site. Yet most attorney bios read like a resume awkwardly dropped onto a webpage, dense credential lists with little sense of who the attorney actually is or why a prospective client should feel confident hiring them. Here are ten practical ways to improve an attorney bio so it actually builds trust and moves a visitor toward contacting the firm.",
